{"shortDescription":"Spot basis values for soybeans were mostly steady at U.S. Midwest elevators on Monday and mixed at processing plants as some crushers stepped up bids to secure immediate supplies while others dropped bids as harvesting was underway in some areas.Basis values are quoted against CBOT futures in cents…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Spot basis values for soybeans were mostly steady at U.S. Midwest elevators on Monday and mixed at processing plants as some crushers stepped up bids to secure immediate supplies while others dropped bids as harvesting was underway in some areas."]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["A processor in Des Moines, Iowa, was bidding 70 cents a bushel over Chicago Board of Trade November futures for soybeans delivered by Saturday, while bids for deliveries later in the month were 30 cents under futures. Bids for soybeans delivered to a Sioux City, Iowa, crusher by Saturday were at a 55-cent premium over deliveries later in September."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["A Lafayette, Indiana, soy crusher dropped its spot basis bid by 10 cents a bushel on Monday for beans delivered by Friday, although the spot bid was 20 to 25 cents higher than bids for beans delivered in the last half of September."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The U.S. Department of Agriculture on Monday said 4% of the Illinois soy crop and 3% of Indiana's crop were harvested as of Sunday, slightly ahead of average, while Iowa's harvest had not yet started."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The National Oilseed Processors Association is due to release its August U.S. crush report on Tuesday. Analysts polled by Reuters, on average, expect last month's crush to dip to 211.553 million bushels, a three-month low."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Corn basis bids at elevators and processors were also mixed